 be the weakest.\n\n**Order size versus forecast.** Real demand averages about 1.046 × forecast.\n- A product 0 unit short costs about 14 (lost margin 6 + penalty 8). An excess unit costs at most 9 if it spoils, and it keeps for 9 days. So ordering above forecast pays off, up to about 1.15×.\n- A product 1 unit short costs about 9 (margin 7 + penalty 2). An excess unit costs about 8 if it spoils, plus 1.0 per day to store, and it keeps only 6 days. The sweet spot is about 1.05–1.1×.\n\n**Each candidate (product 0 / product 1 relative to forecast):**\n- **5:** 1.11 / 1.10, daily. The best balance.\n- **0:** product 0 about 1.14, bought every other day; product 1 1.10, daily. It still pays the fee nearly every day; batching product 0 only adds a little holding.\n- **3:** 1.24 / 1.10, daily. Product 0 is somewhat too high, but excess product 0 is cheap to carry.\n- **1:** 1.19 / 1.19, daily. Product 1 is clearly over-ordered, which means spoilage and storage costs.\n- **4:** 1.20 / 1.12, every other day.\n- **7:** 1.08 / 1.08, every other day. Slightly low.\n- **2:** exactly 1.00 × forecast, so it falls short of the higher real demand and runs short often. Likely bottom half.\n- **6:** every third day (see above). Likely bottom half.\n\nMy most likely top four are 5, 0, 3, then 7 or 4. Candidates 4 and 7 are close, and so are 3 and 1."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4930, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4930}, "output_tokens": 9, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:05:02.314Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWBTEGJZoXLwKDKAzCxA"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "p